# This workspace root holds many unrelated projects. The Spotter
# production webserver build uses `context: ..` (this directory) so its
# Dockerfile can COPY both spotter-frontend/ and
# spotter-infrastructure/webserver/. Everything else must be excluded so
# none of it — most importantly spotter-backend/.env — is ever sent to
# the Docker build context.
#
# Allowlist approach: ignore everything, then un-ignore only the paths the
# production webserver build actually needs.
*

!spotter-frontend
!spotter-frontend/**
!spotter-infrastructure
!spotter-infrastructure/**

# Re-exclude anything under the allowed trees that should never be sent to
# a build context, even by accident.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.git
**/.env
**/.env.*
!spotter-frontend/apps/web/.env.example
!spotter-infrastructure/.env.example
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/*.log

# spotter-backend must never be part of this build context at all — its
# .env (and everything else) stays fully excluded by the leading `*` above.
